     "data": {
      "text/latex": [
       "\\begin{verbatim}\n",
       "argmin(r::AbstractRange)\n",
       "\\end{verbatim}\n",
       "Ranges can have multiple minimal elements. In that case \\texttt{argmin} will return a minimal index, but not necessarily the first one.\n",
       "\n",
       "\\rule{\\textwidth}{1pt}\n",
       "\\begin{verbatim}\n",
       "argmin(f, domain)\n",
       "\\end{verbatim}\n",
       "Return a value \\texttt{x} from \\texttt{domain} for which \\texttt{f(x)} is minimised. If there are multiple minimal values for \\texttt{f(x)} then the first one will be found.\n",
       "\n",
       "\\texttt{domain} must be a non-empty iterable.\n",
       "\n",
       "\\texttt{NaN} is treated as less than all other values except \\texttt{missing}.\n",
       "\n",
       "\\begin{quote}\n",
       "\\textbf{compat}\n",
       "\n",
       "Julia 1.7\n",
       "\n",
       "This method requires Julia 1.7 or later.\n",
       "\n",
       "\\end{quote}\n",
       "See also \\href{@ref}{\\texttt{argmax}}, \\href{@ref}{\\texttt{findmin}}.\n",
       "\n",
       "\\section{Examples}\n",
       "\\begin{verbatim}\n",
       "julia> argmin(sign, -10:5)\n",
       "-10\n",
       "\n",
       "julia> argmin(x -> -x^3 + x^2 - 10, -5:5)\n",
       "5\n",
       "\n",
       "julia> argmin(acos, 0:0.1:1)\n",
       "1.0\n",
       "\\end{verbatim}\n",
       "\\rule{\\textwidth}{1pt}\n",
       "\\begin{verbatim}\n",
       "argmin(itr)\n",
       "\\end{verbatim}\n",
       "Return the index or key of the minimal element in a collection. If there are multiple minimal elements, then the first one will be returned.\n",
       "\n",
       "The collection must not be empty.\n",
       "\n",
       "Indices are of the same type as those returned by \\href{@ref}{\\texttt{keys(itr)}} and \\href{@ref}{\\texttt{pairs(itr)}}.\n",
       "\n",
       "\\texttt{NaN} is treated as less than all other values except \\texttt{missing}.\n",
       "\n",
       "See also: \\href{@ref}{\\texttt{argmax}}, \\href{@ref}{\\texttt{findmin}}.\n",
       "\n",
       "\\section{Examples}\n",
       "\\begin{verbatim}\n",
       "julia> argmin([8, 0.1, -9, pi])\n",
       "3\n",
       "\n",
       "julia> argmin([7, 1, 1, 6])\n",
       "2\n",
       "\n",
       "julia> argmin([7, 1, 1, NaN])\n",
       "4\n",
       "\\end{verbatim}\n",
       "\\rule{\\textwidth}{1pt}\n",
       "\\begin{verbatim}\n",
       "argmin(A; dims) -> indices\n",
       "\\end{verbatim}\n",
       "For an array input, return the indices of the minimum elements over the given dimensions. \\texttt{NaN} is treated as less than all other values except \\texttt{missing}.\n",
       "\n",
       "\\section{Examples}\n",
       "\\begin{verbatim}\n",
       "julia> A = [1.0 2; 3 4]\n",
       "2×2 Matrix{Float64}:\n",
       " 1.0  2.0\n",
       " 3.0  4.0\n",
       "\n",
       "julia> argmin(A, dims=1)\n",
       "1×2 Matrix{CartesianIndex{2}}:\n",
       " CartesianIndex(1, 1)  CartesianIndex(1, 2)\n",
       "\n",
       "julia> argmin(A, dims=2)\n",
       "2×1 Matrix{CartesianIndex{2}}:\n",
       " CartesianIndex(1, 1)\n",
       " CartesianIndex(2, 1)\n",
       "\\end{verbatim}\n"
